**Read:** [Principles of Extractive Metallurgy — Tarun Kumar Kundu, NPTEL](../sources/Principles-of-Extractive-Metallurgy-NPTEL.lingua#r_7VCNEHN5VCQDDQTZ512PSHFZ78), the complete ion-exchange, adsorption, and solution-recovery sequence; [Extração de Ouro: Princípios, Tecnologia e Meio Ambiente — CETEM](../sources/Extracao-de-Ouro-CETEM.lingua#r_5TP6BXRQ7NWKZQZ94WCBQRR8PN), whole relevant adsorption/recovery chapters and their primary methods; [Non-ferrous Metals Industries — European Commission BREF](../sources/Nonferrous-Metals-Industries-BREF.lingua#r_19ZD7KKDWVWM20MXVNCQZJMCDB), a complete applicable solution-treatment/recovery case.

Ion exchange and adsorption involve material-specific sites, solution chemistry, speciation, competing constituents, and transport. An equilibrium isotherm on a selected feed does not alone predict a column's breakthrough or the purity of a recovered product. Capacity needs a defined constituent, basis, state, and test condition.

Separate equilibrium uptake, film/intraparticle transport, flow/contact, axial dispersion, and the moving concentration profile. Time-to-breakthrough depends on the chosen criterion and outlet measurement support. A fit may not distinguish mass-transfer limitations from changing feed speciation or site competition.

Loading, washing, elution/regeneration, material loss/degradation, and recovery form a full cycle. Reagent, water, energy, residuals, and product contamination must be accounted for on that boundary. A high loading-stage removal can coexist with poor recoverable yield or an unsuitable eluate.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete adsorption/ion-exchange case with original equilibrium/kinetic or breakthrough observations. Independently reconcile constituent inventories through the cycle, compare two defensible models and an alternative feed condition, and assess identifiability/uncertainty. Explain which observations distinguish chemical competition, transport, and material aging. Connect the eluate or recovered product to its next purification/conversion duty.

**Continue:** [Evaluate solution recovery through speciation, reaction, kinetics, and final product evidence](Precipitation-cementation-purity-and-product-separation.lingua#r_6FAVZYK3GT4M5NA2AP2KXG3WEA).

